==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|noch}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|noch||until now, still}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*nuh||still|lit=now too}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*nu||now}} + {{m|ine-pro|*-kʷe-||and, also}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/nɔx/|lang=nl}}
* {{audio|Nl-nog.ogg|audio|lang=nl}}
* {{rhymes|ɔx|lang=nl}}
* {{homophone|lang=nl|noch}}

===Adverb===
{{nl-adv}}

# [[still]], as before
#: {{ux|nl|Nu is de auto '''nog''' mooi en schoon, maar na een paar jaar niet meer.|t=Now the car is '''still''' nice and clean, but after a few years it won't be anymore.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Ik heb '''nog''' genoeg aardappelen, ik heb niet meer nodig.|t=I '''still''' have enough potatoes, I don't need more.}}
# {{lb|nl|in negative phrases}} [[yet]]
#: {{ux|nl|Hij is '''nog''' niet gekomen.|t=He has not come '''yet'''.}}
# {{lb|nl|with an amount}} [[more]], in addition
#: {{ux|nl|Ik geef je '''nog''' één kans om het te raden.|t=I'm giving you one '''more''' chance to guess it.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Ik zie '''nog''' twee vliegtuigen.|t=I see two '''more''' planes.}}

